From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:29:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NEMOTKEVerticalDiffusivity: NEMO's TKE scheme as a flavour of
 CATKEVerticalDiffusivity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The base scheme of NEMO's zdftke.F90 (Gaspar et al. 1990; Blanke and Delecluse 1993), with NEMO's
reference namelist as defaults: mixing length √(2e)/N limited by the distance to the sea floor and
the surface (nn_mxl = 2, ln_mxl0), eddy viscosity 0.1 ℓ √e, Richardson-number Prandtl number
(nn_pdl = 1), surface TKE 67.83 u★², dissipation 0.7 e^{3/2}/ℓ, background 1.2e-4 / 1.2e-5 m² s⁻¹,
and enhanced vertical diffusion (100 m² s⁻¹) where N² < 0. No Langmuir or penetration terms (NEMO
switches them off under sea ice).

Built as CATKEVerticalDiffusivity with NEMOMixingLength and NEMOTKEEquation: only new types and
methods, so stock CATKE is unchanged and the models' CATKE plumbing (TKE tracer, implicit TKE step)
applies as is. Own closure fields (mixing length on faces, surface TKE). The mixing length is computed
by one column kernel per time step (two sweeps). Vertically implicit, single closure only.

For the pan-Arctic comparison with GLORYS12 (which runs NEMO's TKE): panarctic-tools patch 084.

